  "production_script": "tools/generate_water_audio.py",
  "environmental_entry_points": [
    "tools/generate_environment_details.py delegates shoreline and all three drip variants",
    "tools/generate_duck_audio.py delegates all three splash variants"
  ],
  "processing": "DC removal, zero-phase high/low-pass filtering, gain toward previous RMS subject to peak ceilings, two-second equal-power crossfades for the three loops and edge fades for cues. River uses tanh soft peak control at four times its RMS before looping, so rare close-mic transients do not force the whole bed too quiet. Cave excerpts retain natural reverberation and background drips. Duck cues use recorded lake-water splashes as foley, not recorded ducks. Original speed and pitch retained; no synthesis, pitch shifting, time stretching or added reverb. Shared environment writer adds final DC correction and 10 ms edge fades."
}
